{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 11 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\nimport java.math.BigInteger;\nimport java.util.Vector;\n\npublic class Main {\n\tpublic static void main(String[] args) {\n\t\tBigInteger MOD = BigInteger.valueOf(998244353);\n\t\t\n\t\tScanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n\t\tlong n = sc.nextLong();\n\t\tlong m = sc.nextLong();\n\t\tlong L = sc.nextLong();\n\t\tlong R = sc.nextLong();\n\n\t\tlong k = R - L + 1;\n\n\t\tif (n * m % 2 == 1) {\n\t\t\tBigInteger exp = BigInteger.valueOf(n * m);\n\t\t\tBigInteger base = BigInteger.valueOf(k);\n\t\t\tSystem.out.println(base.modPow(exp, MOD));\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tlong e, o;\n\t\t\tBigInteger E, O, exp;\n\t\t\te = R / 2 - (L - 1) / 2;\n\t\t\to = k - e;\n\t\t\tE = BigInteger.valueOf(e);\n\t\t\tO = BigInteger.valueOf(o);\n\t\t\texp = BigInteger.valueOf(n * m);\n\t\t\tBigInteger a = E.add(O).modPow(exp, MOD);\n\t\t\tBigInteger b = E.subtract(O).modPow(exp, MOD);\n\t\t\tSystem.out.println(a.add(b).multiply(MOD.add(BigInteger.ONE)).divide(BigInteger.valueOf(2)).mod(MOD));\n\n\t\t}\n\n\t}\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdint>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 998244353LL;\nconst long long INV2 = (MOD + 1) / 2;  // 499122177\n\n// Fast modular exponentiation: (base^exp) % mod\nlong long mod_pow(long long base, long long exp, long long mod) {\n    long long result = 1 % mod;\n    base %= mod;\n    if (base < 0) base += mod;  // ensure non-negative modulo\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if (exp & 1)\n            result = (result * base) % mod;\n        base = (base * base) % mod;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long n, m, L, R;\n    cin >> n >> m >> L >> R;\n\n    long long k = R - L + 1;\n\n    if ((n * m) % 2 == 1) {\n        // odd grid -> answer = k^(n*m) mod MOD\n        long long exp = n * m;\n        long long ans = mod_pow(k % MOD, exp, MOD);\n        cout << ans << endl;\n    } else {\n        // even grid\n        long long e = R / 2 - (L - 1) / 2;   // count of even numbers in [L,R]\n        long long o = k - e;                // count of odd numbers\n\n        long long exp = n * m;\n\n        long long a = mod_pow((e + o) % MOD, exp, MOD);      // (e+o)^exp mod MOD\n        long long b = mod_pow(((e - o) % MOD + MOD) % MOD, exp, MOD); // (e-o)^exp mod MOD\n\n        long long ans = ((a + b) % MOD) * INV2 % MOD;\n        cout << ans << endl;\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\n<confidence>1.0</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.98258376121521, -0.0002992897352669388, -6.556489552167477e-06, -2.7417760065873154e-05, -2.861018856492592e-06, -5.8887653722194955e-05, -0.014247128739953041, -0.011070143431425095, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0351022370159626, -0.10289783775806427, -4.768360213347478e-06, -1.5026377439498901, -0.38708117604255676, -5.280832192511298e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0142378443852067, -0.06698599457740784, -0.004183351527899504, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -8.344646857